🚽 Test case: #196 -- the struct-tag check on an assignment's TARGET
🚽 resolves an array-element target's own tag too, not just a plain
🚽 identifier (PR #248 review, round 3, finding 2's array-element
🚽 sub-case). infer_expression_struct_name() previously had no
🚽 NODE_ARRAY_ACCESS case, so `values[0] = &r;` (values an array of
🚽 struct/union POINTERS) resolved an empty declared tag -- the same
🚽 "unknown" as "confirmed not applicable" conflation, just on the
🚽 destination side this time -- and the whole tag check silently
🚽 skipped.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Rect {
    rizz w;
    rizz h;
};

lit gang Point *PointPtr;

skibidi main {
    gang Rect r;
    r.w = 11;
    r.h = 22;
    PointPtr values[2];
    values[0] = &r;
    yapping("%d %d", values[0].x, values[0].y);
}
